{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515707-got-roped-into-running-a-v5-game","id":1515707,"title":"Got roped into running a v5 game...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-20T18:08:31-07:00","id":1515707,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon8.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Got roped into running a v5 game...","content":"It finally happened, and as I'm not as conversant in post-v20 metaplot/lore as I'd like to be, I'd like to throw out the chronicle notes I have so far for a vibe/consistency check and to pick some brains as to potential relationship mapping and plot hooks.<br /> <br /> - The game, as all my modern nights chronicles, will be set in Louisville. The game's over Discord and three of the players aren't local, so I'm prepared to provide help on local/regional knowledge.<br /> <br /> - Covid and the fallout of the Breonna Taylor protests will take thematic center stage, juxtaposed against a Second Inquisition that is going to be an extremely present, <i>very</i> existential, threat.<br /> <br /> - The local SI is going to be a loose network of rogue operators out of Fort Campbell. They learned about the existence of vampires early, cut their teeth hunting Sabbat and Shepherds of ur-Shulgi in Afghanistan and Iraq, and work with fundie Baptists rather than the Society. The fundies are their eyes and ears, and without the methodology or oversight of the Society, they're going to be incredibly unstable and unpredictable.<br /> <br /> - The catalyzing event for the SI being unusually dangerous in Louisville, is that during the sect war a coterie of Camarilla vampires pilfered some military-grade equipment from Fort Knox and local KY National Guard armories. The SI managed to sweep the theft under the rug, but hunted and captured the vampires responsible, interrogated them, and used that intelligence to hit Elysium in a decapitating raid that killed the city's Prince, Primogen, and court attendees.<br /> <br /> - When Covid lockdowns started, the vampires left standing opted for voluntary torpor, with only the sheriff staying active to &quot;keep the lights on&quot;. When the Breonna Taylor protests started, a whole lot of Anarchs came into the city. Most were just looking for havens and domains, but among them was a pack of Sabbat defectors who couldn't resist the siren song of Camarilla vampires in voluntary torpor, and used the protests as cover to go right back to their old ways.<br /> <br /> - The sheriff wasn't able to assert praxis on their own, or even keep the peace, and the city's already considered a lost cause by the Ivory Tower with no help forthcoming. They settled for negotiating with the new arrivals to fill vacant domains while keeping the Sabbat defectors off the torpid Cams' scent. But really, it was a stalling tactic in hopes the SI would deal with the new arrivals, long enough for the torpid Cams to rise.<br /> <br /> - As of the start of the chronicle, the city's horrendously overpopulated for the heightened risk the SI poses. Nobody has praxis, and the city's unofficially led by a triumvirate: a Setite with ambitions of declaring himself Baron, the sheriff who's actually Hecata, and a Tzimisce who's the ductus of the former Sabbat pack. This is already a recipe for disaster, made worse for the fact the torpid Camarilla are about to start awakening.<br /> <br /> Now, the NPC character hooks I've already thought about...<br /> <br /> Why is the sheriff an Hecata? They're there to babysit a Shallowing, and &quot;joining&quot; the Camarilla was a matter of convenience. They just hit it off with the former Prince, had a skillset suited for the position, and it helps with &quot;the real job&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Setite is a sleazy televangelist megachurch type. So naturally, he's going to have history with the SI as I'm setting it up. I haven't worked out the exact details yet, but I'm thinking something along the lines of him either being on their radar but (still) too high-profile to simply disappear, or an informant. Maybe he's the one that provoked the fundies into vampire hunting to begin with, deeply regrets this, and is trying to talk them back?<br /> <br /> Probably the most predictable of them all, the Tzimisce doesn't give a rat's ass about the Sabbat bullshit, just wants his own damn domain already, and if a couple Cams trip and fall into his tummy along the way it's just good business. I'm not lazy, I'm cunningly subverting expectation by playing it completely straight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 06-20-2023, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T06:47:37-07:00","id":1515859,"title":"","content":"Depending on how the Camarilla operates in your version of V5, maybe the Camarilla vampires awakening find they have been cut off, new lines of communication have been developed anx since the sherrif is Hecata they've been left out in the cold. <br /> <br /> Given the closeness of Cincinnati, I'd also decide what is in control there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T08:19:46-07:00","id":1515866,"title":"","content":"Don't forget the Drowned Legacies. Maybe, as they're digging up the supposed sleeping spots of ancient Camarilla vampires, they find something... else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T15:50:41-07:00","id":1515903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vendrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515707-got-roped-into-running-a-v5-game?p=1515859#post1515859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on how the Camarilla operates in your version of V5, maybe the Camarilla vampires awakening find they have been cut off, new lines of communication have been developed anx since the sherrif is Hecata they've been left out in the cold.<br /> <br /> Given the closeness of Cincinnati, I'd also decide what is in control there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I plan to run the Camarilla, is that in terms of it being past editions' &quot;vampire Technocracy&quot; it's very much a paper tiger. Limited options for transportation and communication simply means Justicars are less capable of exerting influence over individual cities, and Archons less capable of direct intervention to ensure Princes and Primogen toe party lines. So, cities are reverting back to a more &quot;Dark Ages&quot; status quo where sect allegiance and obligation matters far less than whomever holds praxis, and it's ultimately up to who holds praxis to decide how participatory the city is in sectarian politics and regional power plays.<br /> <br /> So where in past years, Louisville would have at least one Archon visit to straighten matters out, now they're on their own. Especially with as you pointed out, an Hecata sheriff who's nominally Camarilla, but still an outsider and therefore someone not to be trusted. The sheriff's &quot;indie cred&quot; is absolutely why the Anarchs didn't just &quot;take care of the problem&quot;.<br /> <br /> Chicago as always has its hands full with its own BS, and from what I know of the v5 metaplot thus far, the Great Lakes Cams are generally consolidating their own cities and looking towards other Great Lakes cities. I've heard Indy got a pseudo write-up in LtSRR, but I have yet to read into it -- but I expect it's yet another &quot;Anarch-run, but the Chicago Cams are sticking their noses in it&quot; scenario. But given how big agritech, pharma, and medical device industries are in Indy, there's a strong argument to be made for it to be a key Camarilla holding they'd be willing to fight to preserve.<br /> <br /> Cinci's a stickier wicket. I've always run it as a Sabbat city, following from Pittsburgh also being Sabbat. Interstate and Ohio River traffic would make the cities poorly defensible, least of all from southern and New England Sabbat (one thing I did in a past chronicle, was have a Sabbat pack that were modern-day river pirates). The Sabbat defector pack would likely be from either Cinci or Pittsburgh. One idea upon which I struck that I like, is Cinci's a Camarilla city care of a Lasombra coup, hence the pack getting the hell out of dodge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't forget the Drowned Legacies. Maybe, as they're digging up the supposed sleeping spots of ancient Camarilla vampires, they find something... else. </div> </div> </div>I've done the &quot;ancient sleeping evil&quot; thing more times already than I like. It's something I'm going the extra mile to avoid. Not to mention, the torpid Cams I mentioned are all going to be ancillae.<br /> <br /> The SI wiped out the elders on the Elysium hit, hence the city being in complete disarray for a decade; the oldest vampire in the city is going to be maybe a century old. The city's vampires going into voluntary torpor was basically just a reaction to the double whammy of an unusually dangerous SI, and Covid -- can't hunt, curfews in place and remote thermometers/FLIR cameras everywhere, online communications monitored, &quot;culture warriors&quot; everywhere, and a highly contagious disease...better to just nap through it and let the SI peter out in the meantime.<br /> <br /> The sheriff was the lone exception. Being an organovore who can feed on Pathos, has its benefits...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T21:09:54-07:00","id":1515926,"title":"","content":"Just I question in this version of Cam you can have members of all the clans or theses three are very particular cases?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T15:15:52-07:00","id":1516263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515707-got-roped-into-running-a-v5-game?p=1515926#post1515926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just I question in this version of Cam you can have members of all the clans or theses three are very particular cases?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm...not entirely sure what you're getting at.<br /> <br /> Also, on thinking about it, the more I <i>really</i> like the idea of Cinci being a Lasombra-controlled, but Camarilla, city as a contrast to Chicago. Basically, having the structure and hierarchy of a Camarilla city, and abiding the Traditions, but embraces the &quot;survival of the fittest&quot; mentality and is very...aggressive...when it comes to dispatching war coteries to nearby cities, using a hybrid of Camarilla and Sabbat tactics as efficiency dictates. Kind of an &quot;indulge yourself but don't shit where you eat, what happens outside Cinci stays outside Cinci&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Thin-bloods would probably be particularly valuable, on account of the limited daywalking and capacity to throw the Second Inquisition off the scent. Especially when all that's needed to keep the Second Inquisition riled up, the locals suppressed, and attention away from Cinci, is the occasional non-lethal Masquerade breach and false flag <i>some place else</i>. Keeping thin-blood loyalty would be simple enough -- just make promises of safety, domain, and status, and actually deliver for the ultra-minority who manage to get back and cover their tracks.<br /> <br /> It'd be an interesting background antagonistic faction, and good answer as to why Louisville doesn't just up and declare itself Anarch: <i>that</i> asshole over there wouldn't hesitate declaring a crusade to put a lackey in the hot seat, they know what they're doing and rewrote the sect war playbook, and inside a week we'd be neck-deep in &quot;Camarilla in name only&quot; and SI. It's a wonder it hasn't happened <i>yet</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T15:38:43-07:00","id":1516268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515707-got-roped-into-running-a-v5-game?p=1516263#post1516263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm...not entirely sure what you're getting at.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant is that normally the Camarilla kindred belong to the seven clans (or not depending on the version), if a Lasombra, a Ministry and a Giovanni are involved in the middle they are exceptions to the rule, but from what I understand there are people who disregard this concept and claim that the Camarilla has members from all clans, I want to know if this is the case.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T17:14:39-07:00","id":1516290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515707-got-roped-into-running-a-v5-game?p=1516268#post1516268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I meant is that normally the Camarilla kindred belong to the seven clans (or not depending on the version), if a Lasombra, a Ministry and a Giovanni are involved in the middle they are exceptions to the rule, but from what I understand there are people who disregard this concept and claim that the Camarilla has members from all clans, I want to know if this is the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a question with a long, complicated answer. The short one is the Camarilla having closed membership is a product of v5, and prior to that it was open to any clan or bloodline save the Giovanni and Baali. The Giovanni formally because of the Promise of 1528, and the Baali informally because no vampire in their right mind is going to tolerate one's presence. How welcome the vampire was, and how trusted they were within the sect, was another question entirely.<br /> <br /> Yes, there were Lasombra in the sect and even Lasombra Princes, prior to v5. Lucita was an Archon before the Convention of Thorns. Giangaleazzo was the most famous Lasombra Prince.<br /> <br /> Relevant to my campaign, the Sheriff won't be Giovanni. They're Nagaraja. As far as the Anarchs go, they're essentially squatters who moved into the city while the Cams were in torpor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T21:20:49-07:00","id":1516314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515707-got-roped-into-running-a-v5-game?p=1516268#post1516268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I meant is that normally the Camarilla kindred belong to the seven clans (or not depending on the version), if a Lasombra, a Ministry and a Giovanni are involved in the middle they are exceptions to the rule, but from what I understand there are people who disregard this concept and claim that the Camarilla has members from all clans, I want to know if this is the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in the Camarilla you had the Lasombra Antitribu, who were full members since the founding of the Sect and were given full respect. They were fairly rare and had to worry about getting hunted by Sabbat, but they were formal members. The Followers of Set, as a clan, were not members of the Camarilla, but members would join the Camarilla. The Giovanni were the only Clan who were not allowed to be full members and instead were given more of an informal membership - as long as they obeyed the rules and did what the Prince wanted, they'd be allowed into the city and essentially given equal treatment, though formally they were still considered &quot;guests.&quot; There were even a handful of Tzimisce in the Camarilla, though they were incredibly rare, tended to keep a low profile. No Baali of course, but they have to keep hidden because nobody likes them.<br /> <br /> The Seven main Clans probably made up something like 95% of the Camarilla's membership, and other clans and bloodlines made up a small fraction, but they existed and the Camarilla would point to them as proof that the organization existed for the good of all vampires, rather than just a select few.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T17:16:33-07:00","id":1516928,"title":"","content":"How is V5? My friends were certainly excited when NWoD came out, but, since then, they haven't mentioned anything about any later versions of Masquerade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T16:17:33-07:00","id":1517520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515707-got-roped-into-running-a-v5-game?p=1516928#post1516928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is V5? My friends were certainly excited when NWoD came out, but, since then, they haven't mentioned anything about any later versions of Masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, it's meh, take it or leave it. If you played VtR, it's basically just VtR with VtM's setting and metaplot. It's not really enough on its own to pick up, unless you've never played past editions or really like VtR. <br /> <br /> The only reason I'm building this as v5, is because I have new players who would do better under v5's clearer, simpler, and more concise mechanics, and won't be bogged down by expectations set by OG VtM. I'll only have one player who's played V20/DAV20; I was in the group with them, and they've never experienced how I run modern nights. So, clean start is best start.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm working on the Tzimisce NPC. I was going to set this NPC up as a &quot;back alley plastic surgeon&quot;, but I actually hit on the idea of them running a &quot;back alley cancer clinic&quot;, using Vicissitude to remove tumors instead of purdy up the mortals. Which could make the NPC's predator type grim reaper, instead of scene queen as I was planning. I personally think it's an interesting idea, but I figured I'd throw it out there for a general vibe check before moving forward.<br /> <br /> Going along with the &quot;post-Covid&quot; theme and a major shallowing being in the city, I was thinking it could be a running thing that morbid and/or death-obsessed vampires are either lured, or just settle, in Louisville.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T08:54:41-07:00","id":1517565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515707-got-roped-into-running-a-v5-game?p=1517520#post1517520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, it's meh, take it or leave it. If you played VtR, it's basically just VtR with VtM's setting and metaplot. It's not really enough on its own to pick up, unless you've never played past editions or really like VtR., .</div> </div> </div> </div>When I read V:tR for the first time, I got the impression that every question that any player ever asked during the past fifteen-years of playing V:tM was answered in that long-book. V:tR really didn't catch on too well, but, I liked it because it was different, but, if confused the long-time V:tM players that knew how to character-engineer and make powerful-characters. Me, I like games about immortality. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-09T13:54:36-08:00","id":1526570,"title":"","content":"Necro it may be, I'm on the cusp of actually running this and figured I'd give an update and crowdsource for feedback and ideas.<br /> <br /> I'm reworking the backstory a bit, and throwing in some stupid shit that happened in past chronicles with my old local group. Now, the beginning of the shitshow was the 2008 Kentucky Derby, which in this past chronicle was...disrupted...by Sabbat PC's being, well, Sabbat PC's. One of the elders' hobbies was horse breeding, one of his horses made it into the Derby, and this elder tasked the PC's with sneaking into Churchill Downs and doping his horse with a little extra blood the night before the race.<br /> <br /> The elder actually had a pretty cunning scheme in mind. His horse had a <i>phenomenally</i> racist name; this elder realized if his racist horse won the Derby, it would cause civil unrest in Louisville and therefore perfect cover for a siege. While, at the same time, giving some of the Louisville Camarilla a severe prestige and influence hit from having to maneuver through the larger social and political ramifications of a horse with a racist name winning the biggest and most famous horse race in the world. So, he tasked the PC pack with the job, knowing they'd be convenient stool pigeons if the whole scheme failed or backfired.<br /> <br /> The pack did as told, but they also had the bright idea of doping every other horse (and overfeeding them) for shits and giggles. All the horses frenzied when the race started, started attacking each other and their jockeys, and several jumped the railing and started attacking spectators in the infield. Being this is a globally-broadcast live sporting event, it turned out to be the biggest public Masquerade breach since the publication of Bram Stoker's <i>Dracula</i>. Needless to say the cammies had their hands full cleaning up the mess and hunting down those responsible, except the Sabbat pack who did it ganked the elder responsible, fled Louisville, and went to ground.<br /> <br /> And being this was on the cusp of the Second Inquisition, and all the old ways just backfired. The SI massively ramped up activities in Louisville, and this culminated in the 2018 Elysium slaughter.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Lasombra performed a mini-Giangaleazzo in Cincinnati, ate or drove out Sabbat of every other clan, and unilaterally declared themselves Camarilla without having delivered a single Sabbat elder to an existing Camarilla vampire. Essentially, flipping off Kevin Jackson, Sierra van Burrace and Talley, the Amici Noctis, and the Inner Council simultaneously. And from there, they've been eyeballing rapid, aggressive expansion in every major metropolitan area nearby -- including Louisville.<br /> <br /> Which brings us to why the Lasombra are so interested in Louisville. I've always played up Waverly Hills Sanatorium's prominence and supernatural legends in my chronicles to varying degrees, and this one will be no different. This time, the entire property is a shallowing, and its morgue is the site of a nihil. Hence, the Sheriff/acting Prince being Nagaraja, and why her ass is parked right in Waverly Hills -- she's there to keep stupid mortals or other vampires from fucking with the nihil, make sure Hecata can use it freely, but most importantly ensure nothing too nasty comes from &quot;the other side&quot;. The Lasombra want access to the nihil so they can fuck with it, make sure Lasombra can use it freely, but most importantly ensure anything too nasty coming from &quot;the other side&quot; is under their control.<br /> <br /> What's happening on that &quot;other side&quot;? well, Covid caused things to get...<i>weird</i>. The Hecata and wraiths expected a Seventh Great Maelstrom, but...the opposite happened. The Tempest subsided, and as if that wasn't ominous enough, the Sea of Shadows <i>froze over</i>. If Great Maelstroms are precipitated by mass death, suffering, hatred, anger, and violence, then something approximating its inverse is appropriate for times of mass suffering, fear, isolation, and dread, but considerably less death than expected. I'm not exactly in love with the idea of calling it the (first) Great Doldrum, but I can't think of any better name right now. Either way, I think it's a fitting supernatural allegory for Covid lockdowns, social distancing, and global fear and uncertainty.<br /> <br /> More to come as I flesh this out further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T09:50:10-08:00","id":1526602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515707-got-roped-into-running-a-v5-game?p=1517520#post1517520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I'm working on the Tzimisce NPC. I was going to set this NPC up as a &quot;back alley plastic surgeon&quot;, but I actually hit on the idea of them running a &quot;back alley cancer clinic&quot;, using Vicissitude to remove tumors instead of purdy up the mortals. Which could make the NPC's predator type grim reaper, instead of scene queen as I was planning. I personally think it's an interesting idea, but I figured I'd throw it out there for a general vibe check before moving forward.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could do it as a sort of 'psychic surgeon' or faith healer angle, to give them cover. &quot;I'm not a Tzimisce, I'm psychic/blessed by god!&quot; Might even be interesting if they're able to fly under the radar of the local SI because they play to expectations of certain religious fringe groups.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T18:23:08-08:00","id":1526646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515707-got-roped-into-running-a-v5-game?p=1526602#post1526602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could do it as a sort of 'psychic surgeon' or faith healer angle, to give them cover. &quot;I'm not a Tzimisce, I'm psychic/blessed by god!&quot; Might even be interesting if they're able to fly under the radar of the local SI because they play to expectations of certain religious fringe groups.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That all got nuked. One of my players' PC's concepts was a Tzimisce with the same background and social niche, so I wrote that NPC out and letting that player fill the niche instead. Now that I know the other players' clans (Hecata, Banu Haqim, and Brujah) I'll be rewriting what I've already done to make for good individual antagonists and character conflicts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}